# Requests for trying every endpoint, in order: register → login → browse → cart → checkout → pay → admin.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5152

### OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### --- Auth (T5) ---

### Register (always a Customer; a "role" in the body is ignored)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "phone": "08012345678"
}

### Login: copy data.token into @token below
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.data.token}}

### Who am I
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Update my profile (name and phone only)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ada King",
  "phone": "08087654321"
}

### No token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Malformed JSON -> 400 INVALID_JSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ada@example.com",

### --- Catalogue (T6, public) ---

### Categories (cached 30 min)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories

### Products: first page, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products

### Products: search, filter and sort
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?search=shirt&minPrice=1000&maxPrice=50000&sortBy=price_asc&page=1&pageSize=5

### Products in one category
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?categoryId=1

### One product (cached 10 min)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/1

### Unknown product -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/99999

### pageSize over 50 / unknown sortBy -> 400 VALIDATION_ERROR
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?pageSize=100&sortBy=cheapest

### minPrice > maxPrice -> 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?minPrice=500&maxPrice=100

### --- Cart (T7, Customer only; log in above first) ---

### My cart: current prices, subtotals, total, and isAvailable per line
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a product (adding it again increases the quantity)
# @name addItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

###
@itemId = {{addItem.response.body.$.data.items[0].id}}

### More than the stock -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 1000
}

### Unknown product -> 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 99999,
  "quantity": 1
}

### Set a line's quantity (0 removes it)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 3
}

### Item not in my cart -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantity": 1
}

### Remove one line -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Empty the cart -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Orders (T8, Customer only) ---

### Put something in the cart first
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 1
}

### Checkout -> 201. Empty cart -> 400; not enough stock -> 409 naming the product
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shippingFullName": "Ada King",
  "shippingPhone": "08087654321",
  "street": "12 Marina Road",
  "city": "Lagos",
  "state": "Lagos"
}

###
@orderId = {{placeOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}

### My orders, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One order with its lines (snapshot name and price)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Someone else's or unknown order -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cancel (Pending only) -> 200, stock returned. Cancelling again -> 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Payments (T10) ---
### Flow: place an order above, initialize, open authorizationUrl in a browser and pay with a Paystack
### test card, then verify. The signed webhook is easier from Postman (postman/ folder), which computes the signature.

### Start a Paystack payment for my Pending order -> authorizationUrl. Not mine -> 404, not Pending -> 409
# @name initPayment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/initialize/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
@reference = {{initPayment.response.body.$.data.reference}}

### Check with Paystack and confirm (safe to repeat): payment Successful + order Paid once actually paid
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/verify/{{reference}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Webhook with a wrong signature -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/payments/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
x-paystack-signature: 0000dead

{
  "event": "charge.success",
  "data": { "reference": "{{reference}}" }
}

### --- Admin (T11) ---
### Log in as the seeded admin. The password is the Seed:AdminPassword user-secret: paste it below, don't commit it.
@adminPassword = paste-the-Seed:AdminPassword-secret-here

# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@ecommerce.local",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

###
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.token}}

### Dashboard: counts by status, revenue (Paid and later), low stock, 5 latest orders. Customer token -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Products, active and inactive (isActive=true/false to filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Create a product (slug made from the name). Unknown category -> 400, same name -> 409
# @name createProduct
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "name": "USB-C Cable 2m",
  "description": "Braided fast-charging cable.",
  "price": 4500,
  "stockQuantity": 50,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "isActive": true
}

###
@productId = {{createProduct.response.body.$.data.id}}

### Update it (full replacement; clears its cache entry)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "categoryId": 1,
  "name": "USB-C Cable 2m",
  "description": "Braided fast-charging cable.",
  "price": 3900,
  "stockQuantity": 45,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "isActive": true
}

### Soft delete -> 204. GET /api/products/{id} is then 404; the admin GET still shows it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Create a category -> 201. Same name (or same slug) -> 409
# @name createCategory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Garden Tools" }

###
@categoryId = {{createCategory.response.body.$.data.id}}

### Rename (clears the category list and every cached product in the category)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Garden & Outdoor" }

### Delete -> 204, or 409 if any product (even inactive) is in it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/categories/{{categoryId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### All orders, optionally by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/orders?status=Pending&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Any customer's order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Change status: Pending -> Cancelled (stock back), Paid -> Processing -> Shipped -> Delivered. Anything else -> 409
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/orders/{{orderId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Cancelled" }

### Customers (read only, no password hashes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/customers?page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
